{"tool_name":"memdock","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"memdock","home":"http://bioinfo3d.cs.tau.ac.il/Memdock/index.html","license":"Not licensed","summary":"An \u03b1-Helical Membrane Protein Docking Algorithm.","addition_date":"2021-12-04T23:15:26.899061Z","last_update_date":"2021-12-04T23:17:43.186246Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:memdock","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"namih@tau.ac.il","name":"Naama Hurwitz","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"wolfson@tau.ac.il","name":"Haim J Wolfson","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein-ligand docking","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0482"},{"term":"Protein-protein docking","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3899"},{"term":"Sorting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3802"}]}],"name":"Memdock","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-0716-1468-6_7","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, Springer Science+Business Media, LLC, part of Springer Nature.Memdock is a tool for docking \u03b1-helical membrane proteins which takes into consideration the lipid bilayer environment. Given two \u03b1-helical membrane located protein molecules, the method outputs a list of potential complexes sorted by energy criteria. The program includes three steps: docking, refinement, and re-ranking of the results. All three docking steps have been customized to the membrane environment in order to improve performance and reduce program run-time. In this chapter, we describe the application of our web server, referred to as Memdock, for prediction of the docking complex for a pair of input membrane protein structures. Memdock is freely available for academic users without registration at http://bioinfo3d.cs.tau.ac.il/Memdock/index.html.","authors":[{"name":"Hurwitz N."},{"name":"Wolfson H.J."